<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felipe VI of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1968">1968</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felipe VI is King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, succeeding on the abdication of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-carlos-i">Juan Carlos I</a> in June 2014. As head of state of the parliamentary monarchy, he made a televised address in October 2017 condemning the unilateral independence referendum held by the Catalan government, the gravest test of the 1978 constitution since the coup attempt of 1981.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/felipe-vi-of-spain.jpg" alt="Felipe VI of Spain" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saeima · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daiga_Mieri%C5%86a_tiekas_ar_Sp%C4%81nijas_karali_-_53814974005_(cropped)-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
